    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>This plugin allows you to accept payments through PaymentAsia&#8217;s Generic gateway in your WooCommerce store.</p>\n<p>Features:<br />\n* Secure payment processing through PaymentAsia<br />\n* Support for multiple currencies<br />\n* Real-time payment notifications<br />\n* Easy configuration<br />\n* Multi-language support</p>\n<h3>Configuration</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Enable the payment method</li>\n<li>Enter your Gateway URL (Production or Sandbox)</li>\n<li>Enter your Shop URL</li>\n<li>Enter your Merchant Token</li>\n<li>Enter your Secret Code</li>\n<li>Save settings</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin files to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/woocommerce-paymentasia-generic</code> directory</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress</li>\n<li>Go to WooCommerce &gt; Settings &gt; Payments</li>\n<li>Find &#8220;Paymentasia Generic&#8221; and click &#8220;Manage&#8221;</li>\n<li>Configure your PaymentAsia credentials</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"what%20is%20paymentasia%3F\">\nWhat is PaymentAsia?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>PaymentAsia is a payment service provider that offers various payment solutions including Generic.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"do%20i%20need%20a%20paymentasia%20account%3F\">\nDo I need a PaymentAsia account?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, you need to sign up for a PaymentAsia merchant account to use this plugin.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.2.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release</li>\n<li>Basic Generic payment processing</li>\n<li>Webhook support</li>\n<li>Multi-language support</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "PaymentAsia Generic payment gateway for WooCommerce.",
